//RS /// #2075: the shard split is weighted by measured cost, and the weight table is
//RS /// machine-checked.
//RS ///
//RS /// A table nobody reads is a second place to remember cost (AGENTS.md I8), and a
//RS /// row naming a target that no longer exists is a weight that silently stopped
//RS /// applying — which is exactly how a 45-minute target stayed the critical path
//RS /// while six jobs looked balanced. So every row must parse, name a real target,
//RS /// and appear once; and the script must report the load it computed.
